From a2adcc9c519c08488b22ebf742ca717f47647467 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elvin Hayatov <AlvinHV@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 11:35:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 38/59] winemac: add GCMouse raw input support

Port Elvin Hayatov's WineHQ MR !11799 at upstream commit
bfa3c0fdc2da180185dd0e542e85e60e120233a2 to WineForge Wine 11.19.
Retain the original implementation and LGPL notice, with Cocoa declaration
context adapted to 11.19 and an internal provenance marker.

Read relative movement through GCMouse when available, retain existing
buttons/scrolling handling, and support UseGCMouse=N for the old input path.
There is no graphics-backend policy or wineserver ABI change.

Validation: narrow winemac build and exact patch replay checks passed.
A physical mouse probe on DXMT recorded 631 new-path raw movements,
working buttons/wheel and no API errors. The user reports prior successful
original-patch game testing on both DXMT and D3DMetal.

Upstream: https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/11799
(cherry picked from commit 8051e02d38c6283eba9c3993992d7129e267518a)
